{
 "_doc": "DEP-06 'An acquire binds once its claim confirms' (strict-lottery-v8): a DisputeAcquire binds iff its claim_txid is confirmed and its input 0 spends the dispute's current lottery outpoint. Judged from the chain alone, from the claim back: the claim must not itself be re-arm shaped (one input, one output, input nSequence a recovery tier's CSV: 144, 1008, 4032 or 8064); its input 0 spends output 0 of a transaction T; while T is re-arm shaped and confirmed, step to the output 0 its input spends (at most 8 rounds); the lottery is this dispute's iff the transaction reached spends the dispute's vault: any outpoint in 'vaults', the vault outpoint of every rung of the governing QuorumBegin's fee ladder (DEP-03), since any rung may be the one that confirmed. On a consistent chain this is the forward round walk's answer: the claim is the spender of the round's lottery outpoint. reason: binds | unconfirmed (claim unknown or not confirmed: judged again later) | not-a-claim (the named transaction is a re-arm spend) | not-this-lottery (final). txids are display-order hex; the 1120-090836 case uses the real txids of 5c4d78fe, 1d89bd45, 46a66b12 and 21910507, and placeholders for the two vaults, 70b0abb3's confiscation, the anchor and the collateral. A transaction absent from 'txs' is unknown to the judge. Shared cl-deposits / deposits-rust vector.",
